---
/* ONE PAGE PER SHARED NAME that many links lead to (19 October 2026). A name several people bear, in a sentence the data cannot decide, used to open the
   people list filtered on the name: a long table. This page opens instead and says which person is which: for every dead person with a page whose
   register name carries the name, the standing, the born year (or "not dated"), the place, the relatives the data records who are dead and have a page, the
   line of the record that produced them, and a link to their page. Everything is read from people.json by tools/run-autolink.py --same-data
   (site/src/data/same-name.json); nothing is added, nothing is said about who is who beyond what a row says.

   WHO IS LISTED. Only a dead person with a page of their own. A living or held-out person, or one born within a hundred years with no death recorded, is
   never listed, and the generator refuses to make this page's data at all if the name has one (so the count in the first sentence cannot be short by
   somebody). A relative who is living or held out is not named. The people list shows a living person as a name and a town; this page shows none.

   NO "AT THE TIME" NOTE. This page carries no era notes: it states no dated place-event of one person. The place is where the register FOUND the person
   (the people list's "Where" column), set beside a born year only as two separate facts; it is not said to be the birthplace.

   INDEXABLE, like the people list: every person on it is dead and public. Not in any menu; the book gives it the chapter of The People (book.json "inherit"). */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../../lib/url.js";
import data from "../../data/same-name.json";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return data.pages.map((p) => ({ params: { slug: p.slug }, props: { page: p } }));
}
const { page } = Astro.props;
const { name } = page;
const exact = page.bearers.filter((b) => b.exact);
const longer = page.bearers.filter((b) => !b.exact);
const STATUS = { connected: "Connected to the line", high: "High interest", interest: "Of interest",
  unplaced: "Unplaced", excluded: "Excluded" };
const plural = (n, one, many) => (n === 1 ? one : many);

const lead = exact.length === 1
  ? `1 person in this archive is called ${name}, and ${longer.length} more carry the name inside a longer one. They are not all the same person; here is how to tell them apart.`
  : `${exact.length} people in this archive are called ${name}. They are not all the same person; here is how to tell them apart.`;
const groups = [
  { id: "called", head: `Called ${name}`, list: exact,
    note: "Their register name reads as this name, with whatever the register adds in brackets to tell them apart." },
  { id: "inside", head: `Carrying ${name} inside a longer name`, list: longer,
    note: `A second given name, a second surname or an initial stands between or after the words, so a page that writes just “${name}” may be using it for one of them.` },
].filter((g) => g.list.length);
---
<Base title={`${name}: telling them apart`} noAutolink
      eyebrow="A name several people share"
      dek={lead}>

<section class="blk">
  <p class="prose">This page does not decide which of them a sentence means. It sets out what the archive's data says of each person who bears the name, so a
    reader can tell them apart; each name opens that person&rsquo;s own page.
    Ordered by standing, then by year. {page.bearers.length} {plural(page.bearers.length, "person", "people")} in all.</p>
  <p class="cap">Only people who have died and have a page are listed. A relative is shown where the data records one who has died and has a page.
    A relationship marked <em>family tree, unverified</em> comes from a user-contributed tree and has not been checked against a record.</p>
</section>

{groups.map((g) => (
  <section class="blk" id={g.id}>
    <h2>{g.head} <span class="cap sn-n">({g.list.length})</span></h2>
    <p class="cap" style="margin-top:6px">{g.note}</p>
    <ol class="sn-list">
      {g.list.map((b) => (
        <li class="sn-one" id={b.slug}>
          <h3><a href={u(`/people/${b.slug}/`)}>{b.name}</a></h3>
          <p class="sn-chips"><span class="chip">{STATUS[b.status] || b.status}</span></p>
          <dl class="sn-facts">
            <dt>Born</dt><dd>{b.born || "not dated"}</dd>
            {b.died && <><dt>Died</dt><dd>{b.died}</dd></>}
            {b.where && <><dt>Found at</dt><dd>{b.where}</dd></>}
            {(b.father || b.mother) && <><dt>Parents</dt><dd>{[b.father, b.mother].filter(Boolean).map((r, i) => (
              <>{i ? "; " : ""}<a href={u(`/people/${r.slug}/`)}>{r.name}</a>{r.tree && <span class="cap sn-t"> (family tree, unverified)</span>}</>))}</dd></>}
            {b.spouses.length > 0 && <><dt>{b.spouses.length === 1 ? "Spouse" : "Spouses"}</dt><dd>{b.spouses.map((r, i) => (
              <>{i ? "; " : ""}<a href={u(`/people/${r.slug}/`)}>{r.name}</a>{r.tree && <span class="cap sn-t"> (family tree, unverified)</span>}</>))}</dd></>}
            {b.children.length > 0 && <><dt>{b.children.length === 1 ? "Child" : "Children"}</dt><dd>{b.children.map((r, i) => (
              <>{i ? "; " : ""}<a href={u(`/people/${r.slug}/`)}>{r.name}</a>{r.tree && <span class="cap sn-t"> (family tree, unverified)</span>}</>))}</dd></>}
            {b.source && <><dt>On the word of</dt><dd>{b.source}</dd></>}
          </dl>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </section>
))}

<section class="blk">
  <p class="cap">Every line here is read from the people list, <a href={u("/people/")}>which has the same people in one table</a>;
    <a href={u(`/people/?q=${encodeURIComponent(name)}`)}>the same list filtered on this name</a> is the longer way round.
    Nothing on this page is a new claim about anyone. &nbsp;·&nbsp; <a href={u("/people/")}>&larr; All the people</a></p>
</section>

<style>
  .sn-n { font-weight: 400; }
  .sn-list { list-style: none; margin: 18px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 420px), 1fr)); }
  .sn-one { border: 1px solid var(--rule); border-radius: 4px; padding: 14px 16px; background: var(--panel); min-width: 0; }
  .sn-one h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.3; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sn-chips { margin: 8px 0 0; }
  .sn-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: max-content 1fr; gap: 4px 14px; margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.45; }
  .sn-facts dt { color: var(--ink-3); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .04em; padding-top: 2px; }
  .sn-facts dd { margin: 0; min-width: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .sn-t { display: inline; margin: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .sn-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; } .sn-facts dd { margin-bottom: 6px; } }
</style>
</Base>
